  "prompt": "Write a function that creates and returns a configuration object with the fields prefix, ssl, port, host, redis, and onConnectionClose. The redis field should contain the Redis connection configuration with host, port, and options. The onConnectionClose field should be initialized to null so a caller can assign a connection-closure handler later.\n\nOnly return the code, don't include any other information, such as a preamble or suffix.",
  "implementation_details": "Language: Javascript. This should be implemented in JavaScript. Create an object with the specified fields. Use standard JavaScript object syntax for configuration. Set onConnectionClose to null and return the configured object.",
